ception (b3-b6), and those of standing and parking (passengers, loading) are covered by stopping, so the union is drv.motion.complete_halt ('at rest at the observation') with p.halt_speed_tolerance. Same mapping as the index row 'No person shall stop, stand or park a vehicle'."}, {"span": "b4", "atoms": ["dev.governs", "dev.stop_sign", "dev.traffic_signal", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "A halt in compliance with law is read through the halts a governing device requires: the subject occupies (rel.occupies) an st.travel_region governed (dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls') by a dev.stop_sign ('regulatory sign requiring a full halt') or by a dev.traffic_signal showing a red indication. dev.governs is not a stand-in for a position: it decides which device controls the region occupied. Same atoms as the index row 'in compliance with law'."}, {"span": "b5", "atoms": ["dev.governs", "dev.human_direction", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "DEF-NRS-484A-180 'every officer authorized to direct or regulate traffic': dev.human_direction 'a person directing traffic and the direction given; role ... police_officer; indication ... stop', governing (dev.governs) a travel region the subject occupies. Same atoms as the index row 'or the directions of a police officer'."}, {"span": "b6", "atoms": ["dev.governs", "dev.railway_signal_or_gate", "dev.stop_sign", "dev.traffic_signal", "dev.yield_sign", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "DEF-NRS-484A-145 'every sign, signal, marking and device ... placed or erected by a public authority or railroad for the purpose of regulating, warning or guiding traffic': the devices whose direction requires a halt -- dev.stop_sign, dev.yield_sign, dev.traffic_signal with a red indication, dev.railway_signal_or_gate with lights flashing or gate lowering or down -- governing (dev.governs) a travel region the subject occupies. 'official' is the legal status of the device, read from its presence (status reading). Same atoms as the index row 'or a traffic control device,'."}, {"span": "b9", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.sidewalk"], "derived": [], "justification": "st.sidewalk is the 'area for pedestrians between roadway and property line' (DEF-NRS-484A-240 'that portion of a highway between the curb lines or the lateral lines of a highway and the adjacent property lines intended for the use of pedestrians'); it is not a stand-in for a crosswalk, which the words do not name. rel.occupies anchors the subject's footprint on it."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "b3", "standard": "necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic", "concepts": ["rel.ahead_behind_in_lane", "rel.surface_gap", "ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic"], "params": ["p.queue_halt_gap"], "convention": "a halt is necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic where a road user of traffic is ahead of the halted vehicle in the same lane within the body gap of a queue of halted vehicles", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [{"span": "b10", "why": "Bicycles, electric bicycles and electric scooters are no vehicles under DEF-NRS-484A-320 ('except: (1) Devices moved by human power ... (2) Electric bicycles ... (4) An electric scooter'), so the subject of this duty is never one of them and the duty is the same whether or not the words of subsection 3 hold.", "scope": "none"}], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle. Engaged at an observation where the subject occupies (rel.occupies) an st.sidewalk region and none of the exceptions holds there: no road user of ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic is ahead of the subject in the same lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) with rel.surface_gap at most p.queue_halt_gap; the subject occupies no st.travel_region governed (dev.governs) by a dev.stop_sign, a dev.yield_sign, a dev.traffic_signal showing circular_red, red_arrow or flashing_red, or a dev.railway_signal_or_gate with lights flashing or gate lowering or down; and no dev.human_direction of role police_officer indicating stop governs a travel region it occupies.", "obligation": "drv.motion.complete_halt(subject; p.halt_speed_tolerance) does not hold: the subject is not at rest while on the sidewalk. A halt there is violated.", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance", "p.queue_halt_gap"], "narrowings": [{"span": "b1", "why": "'A person' who stops, stands or parks a vehicle is read through the vehicle's controlled motion, whoever controls it.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "b3", "why": "'necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic' is read only as a halt behind a road user ahead in the same lane within the queue gap; a halt for a crossing road user that is not ahead in the lane is not read as excused.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "b4", "why": "'in compliance with law' is read only through the halts a governing stop sign or red signal requires; halts other laws require without such a device are not read as excused.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "b6", "why": "'official traffic-control device' is read from the device's presence on the road, its official status presumed.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "The subject car halts with its front half on a sidewalk across a driveway for 30 s; no road user ahead of it, no device or officer governs the region it occupies; no other road user in the scene."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The subject car crosses a sidewalk at a driveway at 3 m/s without halting."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The subject car halts in the roadway lane, its footprint overlapping no sidewalk."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The subject car is on a sidewalk across a driveway, but kin.speed is not observed on this source, so whether it is at rest is unknown.", "masked": ["kin.speed"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The subject car halts with part of its body on the sidewalk while a police officer's stop direction governs the lane it also occupies."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The subject car halts with part of its body on the sidewalk 2 m behind a halted car ahead of it in the same lane."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of tracking sources"}, {"name": "p.queue_halt_gap", "unit": "m", "value": 5.0, "convention": "the gap between bodies to a road user ahead in the same lane within which a halt is a halt behind other traffic: the spacing of halted vehicles in a queue", "source": "jam spacing of halted vehicle queues"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
