{"node_id": "NRS_484B_403_3", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-403-3"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "The driver of a vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "shall not make a U-turn", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "in a business district,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "except at an intersection", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "or on a divided highway", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s6", "text": "where an appropriate opening or crossing place exists.", "role": "exception"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed as one atom; ru.aggregate 'true when the user carries an included class'. 'The driver of' is the relational role DEF-NRS-484A-080 defines ('every person who drives or is in actual physical control of a vehicle'), which the aggregate is not a stand-in for: it is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency reading), so the binder is the vehicle whose conduct is judged. Same mapping as the index row 'The driver of a vehicle'."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.highway"], "derived": ["drv.motion.u_turn"], "justification": "drv.motion.u_turn denotes a road user that 'has turned \"so as to proceed in the opposite direction\": its heading has reversed, \"whether accomplished by one continuous movement or not\"', the definition DEF-NRS-484B-077 ('the turning of a vehicle upon a highway so as to proceed in the opposite direction, whether accomplished by one continuous movement or not'). The concept 'says nothing of the way on which a turns', so the definition's 'upon a highway' is carried beside it: rel.occupies ('a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region') of an st.highway region ('the entire public way between its boundary lines'); st.highway is not a stand-in for the roadway, and the definition names the highway, not the roadway. The index maps 'shall not make a U-turn' to drv.motion.u_turn alone; the highway anchor is added here because the defined word carries it (PLAN.md)."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": [], "justification": "st.intersection: 'the region where two roadways meet, bounded by the prolongation of their edges; a junction where an alley meets another way ... is no intersection', matching DEF-NRS-484A-105 ('the area embraced within the prolongation or connection of the lateral curb lines ... The junction of an alley with a street, road or highway shall not constitute an intersection'). It is not a stand-in for a crosswalk or a stop line, which the words do not name. rel.occupies anchors the subject's own intersection: 'at an intersection' is the reversal made with the footprint overlapping it."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.highway", "st.on_way", "st.median_or_divider"], "derived": [], "justification": "DEF-NRS-484A-070: 'a highway divided into two or more roadways by means of a physical barrier or dividing section'. st.median_or_divider is the 'physical barrier or dividing section between roadways'; st.on_way ties it to 'the public way (a highway region) a structure region lies on'; rel.occupies anchors the subject on that st.highway. Same mapping as the index row 'driven upon a divided highway'. st.on_way is not a stand-in for nearness: the divider lies on the very way the subject occupies."}, {"span": "s6", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.median_or_divider"], "derived": [], "justification": "st.median_or_divider carries an 'opening attribute where a crossover exists': the opening or crossing place in the divider. rel.occupies of a divider region having that attribute is the reversal passing through the crossover. Same atoms as the index row 'except through an opening in the barrier or dividing section or space'. 'appropriate' is the legal status of a feature on the road: the opening's presence is its evidence (observable_reading, status)."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [{"span": "s3", "id": "asm.business_district"}], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle). The rule is engaged where the reading declares asm.business_district for the subject's place; for a reversal of direction it is engaged where that declaration holds at some observation while the reversal is under way (the subject's yaw rate magnitude above p.turn_yaw_rate_tol, within the window of the act behind its recognition).", "obligation": "At the observation at which drv.motion.u_turn(subject; window p.vehicle_turn_window, u_turn_min p.u_turn_heading_min, yaw_tol p.turn_yaw_rate_tol) rises while the subject occupies (rel.occupies) an st.highway region, one of the exceptions holds, else violated: (a) at every observation while the reversal is under way the subject occupies an st.intersection region; or (b) at every observation while it is under way the subject occupies an st.highway region on which (st.on_way) an st.median_or_divider region lies, and at some observation while it is under way the subject's footprint overlaps an st.median_or_divider region on that highway having the opening attribute. Where no reversal is recognized the duty is complied with.", "params": ["p.vehicle_turn_window", "p.u_turn_heading_min", "p.turn_yaw_rate_tol"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "'The driver of a vehicle' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: the duty binds the vehicle whoever or whatever controls it.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s6", "why": "'an appropriate opening or crossing place' is read by the presence of a divider region carrying the opening attribute on the divided highway the subject occupies; its legal suitability is presumed from that presence.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "asm.business_district declared true; the subject vehicle on a two-way street mid-block, with no intersection and no divider anywhere near, reverses its heading by about 180 degrees within 8 s with its yaw rate observed throughout, occupying the highway region."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "asm.business_district declared true; the subject vehicle reverses its heading by about 180 degrees while its footprint overlaps an intersection region at every observation of the turn."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "asm.business_district declared false for every place of the trace; the subject vehicle makes a mid-block reversal of direction."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "asm.business_district declared true; the subject vehicle's heading reverses mid-block but kin.yaw_rate is not observed on this source, so neither the reversal nor its under-way observations can be decided.", "masked": ["kin.yaw_rate"]}, {"name": "occasion_s3", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "The subject begins a mid-block reversal outside the declared business district and crosses into it during the second half of the turn, completing it there; no intersection or divider."}, {"name": "occasion_s3_outside", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The subject is in the declared business district only before the reversal begins; it leaves the district and then makes the whole reversal mid-block outside it."}, {"name": "occasion_s4", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "In the business district the subject begins the reversal inside an intersection region and completes it mid-block beyond the intersection, so it occupies the intersection for part of the turn only; no divider."}, {"name": "occasion_s4_outside", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "In the business district the subject approaches on a lane outside the intersection, enters it, and makes the whole reversal with its footprint overlapping the intersection at every observation while the turn is under way."}, {"name": "occasion_s5", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "In the business district the subject starts its reversal on a stretch whose way carries no divider and finishes it where a divider with an opening lies on the way, passing through the opening; it is on the divided highway for part of the turn only and occupies no intersection."}, {"name": "occasion_s5_outside", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "In the business district the subject, having driven on an undivided stretch before, makes the whole reversal on a highway on which a divider lies, passing through the divider's opening mid-turn."}, {"name": "occasion_s6", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "In the business district, on a divided highway throughout the reversal, the subject's footprint overlaps the divider region with the opening attribute during the middle part of the turn only."}, {"name": "occasion_s6_outside", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "In the business district, on a divided highway throughout, the subject drives through a divider opening region before beginning its reversal and then reverses within one roadway without overlapping any opening while the turn is under way; no intersection."}], "occasion": {"act": "drv.motion.u_turn", "boundary": "window", "window": "window", "under_way": {"words": "make a U-turn", "atoms": ["kin.yaw_rate"], "derived": [], "justification": "kin.yaw_rate is the 'rate of change of heading'; its magnitude above p.turn_yaw_rate_tol tells an observation inside the reversal from one before it began, when the vehicle ran straight on the same region. It is a reading of the road user's motion, not of a place."}, "spans": {"s3": "some_moment", "s4": "throughout", "s5": "throughout", "s6": "some_moment"}}, "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.vehicle_turn_window", "unit": "s", "value": 10.0, "convention": "the longest duration of a turn by a motor vehicle at a junction or into or out of a driveway, from the start of its heading change to its end, including the crossing of opposing lanes", "source": "observed turning-manoeuvre durations of passenger cars at urban junctions"}, {"name": "p.u_turn_heading_min", "unit": "deg", "value": 135.0, "convention": "the smallest heading change magnitude over the turn window at which a turn counts as a reversal of direction", "source": "geometric convention separating a turn (about 90 degrees) from a reversal (about 180 degrees)"}, {"name": "p.turn_yaw_rate_tol", "unit": "deg/s", "value": 3.0, "convention": "the yaw-rate magnitude at or below which a road user's heading counts as no longer turning: the yaw-rate noise floor of the source", "source": "yaw-rate noise of vehicle inertial and tracking sources"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_407", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-407"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "A vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "shall not be turned so as to proceed in the opposite direction", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "upon any curve,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "or upon the approach to or near the crest of a grade,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "where such vehicle cannot be seen by the driver of any other vehicle approaching from either direction within 500 feet.", "role": "condition"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, one atom; same mapping as the index row 'A vehicle'."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": [], "derived": ["drv.motion.u_turn"], "justification": "drv.motion.u_turn denotes a road user that 'has turned \"so as to proceed in the opposite direction\": its heading has reversed', the very words of the span; the reversal 'whether accomplished by one continuous movement or not' is denoted. 'be turned' by the one at the controls is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency reading)."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.roadway", "st.curvature"], "derived": [], "justification": "st.curvature is the 'horizontal curvature of the roadway at a point, as a magnitude (1/m, never negative): a bend to either hand has the same value'; 'any curve' names the feature without a size, so it is read as the curvature at the subject's place standing clear of zero, above p.curvature_resolution, which names only the source's resolution. rel.occupies of an st.roadway region ('the part of a highway improved for vehicular traffic') anchors the curve to the way the subject is upon. st.curvature is the road's geometry, not the vehicle's yaw (kin.yaw_rate is 'not a stand-in for road curvature')."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["st.crest", "st.region_geometry"], "derived": [], "justification": "st.crest is 'the place on a roadway's longitudinal profile where the slope changes from rising to falling in the direction of travel, carried as a region with a reference point and a boundary, so the ground distance from a road user to it is read through st.region_geometry' -- 'the crest of a grade'. st.region_geometry gives 'the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it'; the approach to or nearness to the crest is that distance at most p.crest_near_reach. st.crest is not a stand-in for the slope at a point (st.grade) nor for the view (st.sight_distance), which s5 reads on its own."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": ["st.sight_distance"], "derived": [], "justification": "st.sight_distance is 'the distance along the road within which a vehicle at a point and another vehicle on the road could see each other ... both the view of approaching traffic from that point and its being seen by drivers approaching it, whether or not any road user is there': 'such vehicle cannot be seen by the driver of any other vehicle approaching from either direction within 500 feet' is that distance at the subject's place below 500 ft. It is not a stand-in for whether an actual road user saw another (rel.visible): the words state what could be seen at the place, whether or not another vehicle is present, so no other vehicle is quantified (perception reading)."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle). The rule is engaged at an observation where, at that one observation, (i) the subject occupies an st.roadway region and st_curvature at its place exceeds p.curvature_resolution, or the ground distance (st.region_geometry) from its body to an st.crest region is at most p.crest_near_reach; and (ii) st.sight_distance at its place is below 500 ft. For a reversal of direction, it is engaged where (i) and (ii) hold together at some one observation while the reversal is under way (yaw rate magnitude above p.turn_yaw_rate_tol, within the act's window behind its recognition).", "obligation": "drv.motion.u_turn(subject; window p.vehicle_turn_window, u_turn_min p.u_turn_heading_min, yaw_tol p.turn_yaw_rate_tol) does not rise: a reversal recognized where the rule is engaged is a violation; otherwise complied with.", "params": ["p.vehicle_turn_window", "p.u_turn_heading_min", "p.turn_yaw_rate_tol", "p.curvature_resolution", "p.crest_near_reach"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s2", "why": "'be turned' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion, whoever or whatever is at the controls.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s4", "why": "'upon the approach to or near the crest' is read as the subject's body within p.crest_near_reach of the crest region on either side of it; the direction of motion toward the crest is not required, since 'near' covers both sides.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "s5", "why": "'cannot be seen by the driver of any other vehicle approaching from either direction' is read through the sight distance of the subject's place (what could be seen at a place), not through any actual driver's perception.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "perception"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "The subject vehicle on a roadway bend (curvature well above the resolution) where st.sight_distance is 100 m reverses its heading by about 180 degrees within 8 s, yaw rate observed."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "On the same bend with st.sight_distance 80 m the subject drives through without reversing; no other road user in the scene."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The subject reverses direction on a straight, level roadway (curvature at or below the resolution) with no crest within the reach and st.sight_distance 400 m."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The subject reverses direction on a roadway bend; st.sight_distance is not observed on this source, so whether the condition holds is unknown.", "masked": ["st.sight_distance"]}, {"name": "occasion_s3", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "The subject begins its reversal on a straight stretch and the second half of the turn takes place where the roadway curves; sight distance is 100 m throughout; no crest near."}, {"name": "occasion_s3_outside", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The subject is on the bend (sight distance 100 m) only before the reversal begins; it makes the whole reversal on the straight stretch beyond, where sight distance is 400 m; no crest near."}, {"name": "occasion_s4", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "On a straight roadway the subject begins its reversal farther than the reach from a crest and ends it within the reach, where sight distance is 90 m."}, {"name": "occasion_s4_outside", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The subject passes within the reach of a crest (sight 90 m) before the reversal begins and makes the whole reversal on a straight level stretch far beyond it, where sight distance is 400 m."}, {"name": "occasion_s5", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "On a bend the subject begins its reversal where sight distance is 200 m, and during the turn moves to where it is 120 m."}, {"name": "occasion_s5_outside", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "On a bend the subject passes a spot where sight distance is 120 m before the reversal begins, then makes the whole reversal where sight distance is 250 m."}], "occasion": {"act": "drv.motion.u_turn", "boundary": "window", "window": "window", "under_way": {"words": "be turned so as to proceed in the opposite direction", "atoms": ["kin.yaw_rate"], "derived": [], "justification": "kin.yaw_rate is the 'rate of change of heading'; its magnitude above p.turn_yaw_rate_tol tells an observation inside the reversal from one before it began, when the vehicle ran on the same bend or near the same crest without turning."}, "spans": {"s3": "some_moment", "s4": "some_moment", "s5": "some_moment"}}, "literals": [{"span": "s5", "text": "500 feet", "value": 500, "unit": "ft"}], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.vehicle_turn_window", "unit": "s", "value": 10.0, "convention": "the longest duration of a turn by a motor vehicle at a junction or into or out of a driveway, from the start of its heading change to its end, including the crossing of opposing lanes", "source": "observed turning-manoeuvre durations of passenger cars at urban junctions"}, {"name": "p.u_turn_heading_min", "unit": "deg", "value": 135.0, "convention": "the smallest heading change magnitude over the turn window at which a turn counts as a reversal of direction", "source": "geometric convention separating a turn (about 90 degrees) from a reversal (about 180 degrees)"}, {"name": "p.turn_yaw_rate_tol", "unit": "deg/s", "value": 3.0, "convention": "the yaw-rate magnitude at or below which a road user's heading counts as no longer turning: the yaw-rate noise floor of the source", "source": "yaw-rate noise of vehicle inertial and tracking sources"}, {"name": "p.curvature_resolution", "unit": "1/m", "value": 0.0005, "convention": "the horizontal curvature at or below which a mapped roadway reads as straight: the curvature resolution of map centrelines (a radius of about two kilometres)", "source": "HD-map centreline curvature resolution"}, {"name": "p.crest_near_reach", "unit": "m", "value": 150.0, "convention": "the ground distance from a road user's body to a crest within which the road user is on the approach to or near the crest: the length of a crest vertical curve over which forward sight is restricted, about the stopping sight distance at 90 km/h", "source": "AASHTO Green Book, stopping sight distance and crest vertical curve design"}], "gaps": [], "gap_resolutions": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_410_o1", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-410"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "A person,", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "except when stopping, standing or parking where no parking is permitted,", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "shall not start a vehicle which is stopped, standing or parked on a highway", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "nor enter upon a highway", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "unless and until such movement can be made with safety.", "role": "standard"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'A person' who starts a vehicle is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency reading), so the binder is the vehicle, the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; same mapping as the index row 'A person'."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.curb_zone", "dev.regulatory_sign", "dev.governs", "st.travel_region", "prim.conditions_hold"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "'stopping, standing or parking' (DEF-NRS-484A-260 'any halting, even momentarily, of a vehicle'; DEF-NRS-484A-250 'the halting of a vehicle'; DEF-NRS-484A-155 'the standing of a vehicle') together denote every halt, drv.motion.complete_halt ('at rest at the observation'), read at the observation before the start. 'where no parking is permitted' is a place a no-parking restriction marks: an st.curb_zone of kind no_parking, no_stopping or fire_lane or a curb painted red, which the vehicle's footprint overlaps (rel.occupies), or an st.travel_region it occupies that a dev.regulatory_sign of code no_parking, no_standing or no_stopping governs (dev.governs) with its conditions holding (prim.conditions_hold). The sign is a condition, not a manoeuvre (its not-a-stand-in clause does not apply); the posted or painted feature is the evidence of the restriction (status reading)."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "rel.occupies", "st.highway"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "'a vehicle' is the admitted aggregate. 'stopped, standing or parked' is every halt (the three definitions' union: DEF-NRS-484A-260 'any halting, even momentarily', DEF-NRS-484A-250 'the halting of a vehicle', DEF-NRS-484A-155 'the standing of a vehicle'; their exclusions -- conflict or device halts, passenger and loading halts -- intersect only on purposes no conduct shows), drv.motion.complete_halt with p.halt_speed_tolerance. 'start' is the observation at which complete_halt ceases to hold, having held at the previous one. 'on a highway' is rel.occupies of an st.highway region ('the entire public way between its boundary lines', matching DEF-NRS-484A-095 'the entire width between the boundary lines'), at the previous observation."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "s5", "standard": "such movement can be made with safety", "concepts": ["prim.closest_approach_within", "prim.closest_approach_distance"], "params": ["p.conflict_horizon", "p.conflict_centre_clearance"], "convention": "traffic-conflict technique: a movement is made with safety where, at its onset, no other road user's centre is predicted under constant velocities to come within the conflict centre clearance of the subject's centre within the time-to-collision horizon", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle. Engaged at an observation at which the subject starts: drv.motion.complete_halt(subject; p.halt_speed_tolerance) held at the previous observation while the subject occupied an st.highway region, and does not hold at this observation; and the exception does not hold: at the previous observation 