{"node_id": "NRS_484B_440_1_o1", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-440-1"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "a1", "text": "Upon any highway", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "a2", "text": "outside of a business or residence district", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "a3", "text": "no person shall stop, park or leave standing any vehicle,", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "a4", "text": "whether attended or unattended,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "a5", "text": "upon the paved or main-traveled part of the highway", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "a6", "text": "when it is practicable to stop, park or so leave such vehicle off such part of the highway,", "role": "standard"}, {"id": "a7", "text": "but in every event an unobstructed width of the highway opposite a standing vehicle shall be left", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "a8", "text": "for the free passage of other vehicles", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "a9", "text": "and a clear view of such stopped vehicles shall be available from a distance of 200 feet in each direction upon such highway.", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "a10", "text": "This section shall not apply to the driver of any vehicle which is disabled while on the paved or main-traveled portion of a highway in such manner and to such extent that it is impossible to avoid stopping and temporarily leaving such disabled vehicle in such position.", "role": "exception"}], "elements": [{"span": "a1", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.highway"], "derived": [], "justification": "st.highway is 'the entire public way between its boundary lines' (DEF-NRS-484A-095 'the entire width between the boundary lines of every way'); rel.occupies anchors the subject on it. Same mapping as the index row 'on any highway'."}, {"span": "a3", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "'any vehicle' is the admitted aggregate. 'stop, park or leave standing' together denote every halt: DEF-NRS-484A-260 'any halting, even momentarily, of a vehicle, whether occupied or not', DEF-NRS-484A-250 'the halting of a vehicle, whether occupied or not', DEF-NRS-484A-155 'the standing of a vehicle'; their exclusions (a halt to avoid conflict or on a device's direction; one receiving or discharging passengers; one loading) intersect only on purposes no conduct shows, so the union is drv.motion.complete_halt ('at rest at the observation') with p.halt_speed_tolerance. 'no person' is read through the vehicle's conduct (agency)."}, {"span": "a5", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.roadway"], "derived": [], "justification": "st.roadway is 'the part of a highway improved for vehicular traffic, excluding shoulder': the paved or main-traveled part. The roadway is not a stand-in for the sidewalk, and 'not on the roadway' includes the shoulder, which is the place off that part the words contrast it with. rel.occupies anchors the subject's footprint on it."}, {"span": "a10", "atoms": ["kin.engine_running", "sig.hazard"], "derived": [], "justification": "Nearest atoms only, shown to mark the gap: kin.engine_running is 'not a stand-in for motion or a halt' and an engine stopped does not make a vehicle unable to move; sig.hazard is a signal a road user emits, not the condition of the vehicle. Neither denotes a vehicle disabled so that it is impossible to avoid stopping; the span is filed as an atom gap."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "a6", "standard": "practicable to stop, park or so leave such vehicle off such part of the highway", "concepts": ["st.shoulder", "st.parking_space", "st.region_geometry", "st.on_way"], "params": ["p.offroad_refuge_reach"], "convention": "leaving a vehicle off the main-traveled part is practicable where a shoulder or a parking bay lies on the same way within the distance a vehicle covers when braking from a rural speed at a comfortable deceleration", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [{"span": "a2", "id": "asm.business_or_residence_district"}], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [{"span": "a4", "why": "The duty is the same whether or not a person is with the vehicle: the words say so expressly.", "scope": "none"}], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle. Engaged at an observation where the subject occupies an st.highway region, the reading does not declare asm.business_or_residence_district for its place (declared false), the subject occupies an st.roadway region, and an st.shoulder or st.parking_space region lies on the same highway (st.on_way) within ground distance (st.region_geometry) p.offroad_refuge_reach of the subject's body. Not engaged where the subject is disabled so that it is impossible to avoid stopping (gap).", "obligation": "drv.motion.complete_halt(subject; p.halt_speed_tolerance) does not hold: the subject is not at rest on the roadway. A halt there is violated.", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance", "p.offroad_refuge_reach"], "narrowings": [{"span": "a3", "why": "'no person shall stop, park or leave standing' is read through the vehicle's conduct, whoever controls it.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "a6", "why": "'practicable' is read as the presence of a shoulder or bay on the same way within the reach; whether that place is occupied or wide enough is not read.", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "District declared false; the subject car halts in the roadway lane of a rural highway for 60 s while a paved shoulder lies on the same way 2 m from its body."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "District declared false; the subject car drives along the roadway beside the shoulder at 20 m/s without halting."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "asm.business_or_residence_district declared true for the subject's place; it halts in the roadway lane."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "District declared false; the subject car is in the roadway lane beside a shoulder, but kin.speed is not observed on this source.", "masked": ["kin.speed"]}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of tracking sources"}, {"name": "p.offroad_refuge_reach", "unit": "m", "value": 100.0, "convention": "the ground distance from a halted vehicle's body to a shoulder or bay off the main-traveled part within which leaving the vehicle there is practicable: the braking distance from a rural speed of about 25 m/s at a comfortable deceleration of 3.4 m/s^2", "source": "AASHTO Green Book braking distance model"}], "gaps": [{"span": "a10", "kind": "atom", "proposal": "`ru.disabled` | the vehicle cannot move under its own power (a breakdown, damage, a flat tyre), as the source records it **Not a stand-in for:** a vehicle at rest with its engine stopped, or one showing hazard lamps -- the condition is not a halt and not a signal | general", "nearest": "kin.engine_running (Not a stand-in for: motion or a halt -- a vehicle stands with its engine running and rolls with it stopped; an engine off is not a vehicle unable to move); sig.hazard (a signal a road user emits, not the vehicle's condition)"}], "gap_resolutions": []}
