t it is impossible to avoid stopping (gap).", "obligation": "st.sight_distance at the subject's place is at least 200 ft. Otherwise violated.", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "a9", "why": "'in each direction' is read through the one sight distance of the place, which the atom states for the view of and from traffic approaching it; the two directions are not measured apart.", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "District declared false; the subject car stands in the roadway just beyond a crest where st.sight_distance is 40 m."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "District declared false; the subject car stands in the roadway on a straight level stretch where st.sight_distance is 300 m."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "asm.business_or_residence_district declared true for the subject's place; it stands in the roadway where sight distance is 40 m."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "District declared false; the subject car stands in the roadway; st.sight_distance is not observed on this source.", "masked": ["st.sight_distance"]}], "literals": [{"span": "a9", "text": "200 feet", "value": 200, "unit": "ft"}], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of tracking sources"}], "gaps": [{"span": "a10", "kind": "atom", "proposal": "`ru.disabled` | the vehicle cannot move under its own power (a breakdown, damage, a flat tyre), as the source records it **Not a stand-in for:** a vehicle at rest with its engine stopped, or one showing hazard lamps -- the condition is not a halt and not a signal | general", "nearest": "kin.engine_running (Not a stand-in for: motion or a halt -- a vehicle stands with its engine running and rolls with it stopped; an engine off is not a vehicle unable to move); sig.hazard (a signal a road user emits, not the vehicle's condition)"}], "gap_resolutions": []}

{"node_id": "NRS_484B_450_1a", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-450-1a"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "b1", "text": "A person", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "b2", "text": "shall not stop, stand or park a vehicle,", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "b3", "text": "except when necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic", "role": "standard"}, {"id": "b4", "text": "or in compliance with law", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "b5", "text": "or the directions of a police officer", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "b6", "text": "or official traffic-control device,", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "b7", "text": "in any of the following places:", "role": "boilerplate"}, {"id": "b8", "text": "Except as otherwise provided in subsection 3,", "role": "boilerplate"}, {"id": "b9", "text": "on a sidewalk.", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "b10", "text": "A person may park a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter on a sidewalk provided that the bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter does not impede the normal and reasonable movement of pedestrians on the sidewalk.", "role": "exception"}], "elements": [{"span": "b1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'A person' who stops, stands or parks a vehicle is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency reading): the binder is the vehicle, the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; same mapping as the index row 'A person'."}, {"span": "b2", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "'a vehicle' is the admitted aggregate. 'stop, stand or park' together denote every halt: DEF-NRS-484A-260 'any halting, even momentarily, of a vehicle, whether occupied or not', DEF-NRS-484A-250 'the halting of a vehicle, whether occupied or not', DEF-NRS-484A-155 'the standing of a vehicle'; the exclusion of DEF-NRS-484A-260 is the law's own exception (b3-b6), and those of standing and parking (passengers, loading) are covered by stopping, so the union is drv.motion.complete_halt ('at rest at the observation') with p.halt_speed_tolerance. Same mapping as the index row 'No person shall stop, stand or park a vehicle'."}, {"span": "b4", "atoms": ["dev.governs", "dev.stop_sign", "dev.traffic_signal", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "A halt in compliance with law is read through the halts a governing device requires: the subject occupies (rel.occupies) an st.travel_region governed (dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls') by a dev.stop_sign ('regulatory sign requiring a full halt') or by a dev.traffic_signal showing a red indication. dev.governs is not a stand-in for a position: it decides which device controls the region occupied. Same atoms as the index row 'in compliance with law'."}, {"span": "b5", "atoms": ["dev.governs", "dev.human_direction", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "DEF-NRS-484A-180 'every officer authorized to direct or regulate traffic': dev.human_direction 'a person directing traffic and the direction given; role ... police_officer; indication ... stop', governing (dev.governs) a travel region the subject occupies. Same atoms as the index row 'or the directions of a police officer'."}, {"span": "b6", "atoms": ["dev.governs", "dev.railway_signal_or_gate", "dev.stop_sign", "dev.traffic_signal", "dev.yield_sign", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "DEF-NRS-484A-145 'every sign, signal, marking and device ... placed or erected by a public authority or railroad for the purpose of regulating, warning or guiding traffic': the devices whose direction requires a halt -- dev.stop_sign, dev.yield_sign, dev.traffic_signal with a red indication, dev.railway_signal_or_gate with lights flashing or gate lowering or down -- governing (dev.governs) a travel region the subject