{"node_id": "NRS_484B_450_1a", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-450-1a"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "b1", "text": "A person", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "b2", "text": "shall not stop, stand or park a vehicle,", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "b3", "text": "except when necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic", "role": "standard"}, {"id": "b4", "text": "or in compliance with law", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "b5", "text": "or the directions of a police officer", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "b6", "text": "or official traffic-control device,", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "b7", "text": "in any of the following places:", "role": "boilerplate"}, {"id": "b8", "text": "Except as otherwise provided in subsection 3,", "role": "boilerplate"}, {"id": "b9", "text": "on a sidewalk.", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "b10", "text": "A person may park a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter on a sidewalk provided that the bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter does not impede the normal and reasonable movement of pedestrians on the sidewalk.", "role": "exception"}], "elements": [{"span": "b1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'A person' who stops, stands or parks a vehicle is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency reading): the binder is the vehicle, the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; same mapping as the index row 'A person'."}, {"span": "b2", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "'a vehicle' is the admitted aggregate. 'stop, stand or park' together denote every halt: DEF-NRS-484A-260 'any halting, even momentarily, of a vehicle, whether occupied or not', DEF-NRS-484A-250 'the halting of a vehicle, whether occupied or not', DEF-NRS-484A-155 'the standing of a vehicle'; the exclusion of DEF-NRS-484A-260 is the law's own exception (b3-b6), and those of standing and parking (passengers, loading) are covered by stopping, so the union is drv.motion.complete_halt ('at rest at the observation') with p.halt_speed_tolerance. Same mapping as the index row 'No person shall stop, stand or park a vehicle'."}, {"span": "b4", "atoms": ["dev.governs", "dev.stop_sign", "dev.traffic_signal", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "Nearest atoms only, shown to mark the gap: a halt a governing dev.stop_sign or red dev.traffic_signal requires of a travel region the subject occupies (dev.governs, rel.occupies, st.travel_region) is one halt in compliance with law, but 'law' also requires halts no device shows (yielding to oncoming traffic before a turn, to an emergency vehicle, to a school bus), and the formula language composes only named rules (rule, ruleApplies), never whether some engaged rule of the set requires the halt. Same atoms as the index row 'in compliance with law'; the words carry operator gap smoke31-1111-0039:G22."}, {"span": "b5", "atoms": ["dev.governs", "dev.human_direction", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "DEF-NRS-484A-180 'every officer authorized to direct or regulate traffic': dev.human_direction 'a person directing traffic and the direction given; role ... police_officer; indication ... stop', governing (dev.governs) a travel region the subject occupies. Same atoms as the index row 'or the directions of a police officer'."}, {"span": "b6", "atoms": ["dev.governs", "dev.railway_signal_or_gate", "dev.stop_sign", "dev.traffic_signal", "dev.yield_sign", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "DEF-NRS-484A-145 'every sign, signal, marking and device ... placed or erected by a public authority or railroad for the purpose of regulating, warning or guiding traffic': the devices whose direction requires a halt -- dev.stop_sign, dev.yield_sign, dev.traffic_signal with a red indication, dev.railway_signal_or_gate with lights flashing or gate lowering or down -- governing (dev.governs) a travel region the subject occupies. 'official' is the legal status of the device, read from its presence (status reading). Same atoms as the index row 'or a traffic control device,'."}, {"span": "b9", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.sidewalk"], "derived": [], "justification": "st.sidewalk is the 'area for pedestrians between roadway and property line' (DEF-NRS-484A-240 'that portion of a highway between the curb lines or the lateral lines of a highway and the adjacent property lines intended for the use of pedestrians'); it is not a stand-in for a crosswalk, which the words do not name. rel.occupies anchors the subject's footprint on it."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "b3", "standard": "necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic", "concepts": ["rel.ahead_behind_in_lane", "rel.surface_gap"], "params": ["p.queue_halt_gap"], "convention": "a halt is necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic where a road user of traffic is ahead of the halted vehicle in the same lane within the body gap of a queue of halted vehicles", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [{"span": "b10", "why": "Bicycles, electric bicycles and electric scooters are no vehicles under DEF-NRS-484A-320 ('except: (1) Devices moved by human power ... (2) Electric bicycles ... (4) An electric scooter'), so the subject of this duty is never one of them and the duty is the same whether or not the words of subsection 3 hold.", "scope": "none"}], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle. Engaged at an observation where the subject occupies (rel.occupies) an st.sidewalk region and none of the exceptions holds there: no other road user of any class (DEF-NRS-484A-285 'traffic' counts 'pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances') is ahe