t it is impossible to avoid stopping (gap).", "obligation": "st.sight_distance at the subject's place is at least 200 ft. Otherwise violated.", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "a9", "why": "'in each direction' is read through the one sight distance of the place, which the atom states for the view of and from traffic approaching it; the two directions are not measured apart.", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "District declared false; the subject car stands in the roadway just beyond a crest where st.sight_distance is 40 m."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "District declared false; the subject car stands in the roadway on a straight level stretch where st.sight_distance is 300 m."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "asm.business_or_residence_district declared true for the subject's place; it stands in the roadway where sight distance is 40 m."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "District declared false; the subject car stands in the roadway; st.sight_distance is not observed on this source.", "masked": ["st.sight_distance"]}], "literals": [{"span": "a9", "text": "200 feet", "value": 200, "unit": "ft"}], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of tracking sources"}], "gaps": [{"span": "a10", "kind": "atom", "proposal": "`ru.disabled` | the vehicle cannot move under its own power (a breakdown, damage, a flat tyre), as the source records it **Not a stand-in for:** a vehicle at rest with its engine stopped, or one showing hazard lamps -- the condition is not a halt and not a signal | general", "nearest": "kin.engine_running (Not a stand-in for: motion or a halt -- a vehicle stands with its engine running and rolls with it stopped; an engine off is not a vehicle unable to move); sig.hazard (a signal a road user emits, not the vehicle's condition)"}], "gap_resolutions": []}

{"node_id": "NRS_484B_450_1a", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-450-1a"], "subject": {"binder": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "b1", "text": "A person", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "b2", "text": "shall not stop, stand or park a vehicle,", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "b3", "text": "except when necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic", "role": "standard"}, {"id": "b4", "text": "or in compliance with law", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "b5", "text": "or the directions of a police officer", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "b6", "text": "or official traffic-control device,", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "b7", "text": "in any of the following places:", "role": "boilerplate"}, {"id": "b8", "text": "Except as otherwise provided in subsection 3,", "role": "boilerplate"}, {"id": "b9", "text": "on a sidewalk.", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "b10", "text": "A person may park a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter on a sidewalk provided that the bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter does not impede the normal and reasonable movement of pedestrians on the sidewalk.", "role": "exception"}], "elements": [{"span": "b1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'A person' who stops, stands or parks a vehicle is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency reading): the binder is the vehicle, the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; same mapping as the index row 'A person'."}, {"span": "b2", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": ["drv.motion.complete_halt"], "justification": "'a vehicle' is the admitted aggregate. 'stop, stand or park' together denote every halt: DEF-NRS-484A-260 'any halting, even momentarily, of a vehicle, whether occupied or not', DEF-NRS-484A-250 'the halting of a vehicle, whether occupied or not', DEF-NRS-484A-155 'the standing of a vehicle'; the exclusion of DEF-NRS-484A-260 is the law's own exception (b3-b6), and those of standing and parking (passengers, loading) are covered by stopping, so the union is drv.motion.complete_halt ('at rest at the observation') with p.halt_speed_tolerance. Same mapping as the index row 'No person shall stop, stand or park a vehicle'."}, {"span": "b4", "atoms": ["dev.governs", "dev.stop_sign", "dev.traffic_signal", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "Nearest atoms only, shown to mark the gap: a halt a governing dev.stop_sign or red dev.traffic_signal requires of a travel region the subject occupies (dev.governs, rel.occupies, st.travel_region) is one halt in compliance with law, but 'law' also requires halts no device shows (yielding to oncoming traffic before a turn, to an emergency vehicle, to a school bus), and the formula language composes only named rules (rule, ruleApplies), never whether some engaged rule of the set requires the halt. Same atoms as the index row 'in compliance with law'; the words carry operator gap smoke31-1111-0039:G22."}, {"span": "b5", "atoms": ["dev.governs", "dev.human_direction", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "DEF-NRS-484A-180 'every officer authorized to direct or regulate traffic': dev.human_direction 'a person directing traffic and the direction given; role ... police_officer; indication ... stop', governing (dev.governs) a travel region the subject occupies. Same atoms as the index row 'or the directions of a police officer'."}, {"span": "b6", "atoms": ["dev.governs", "dev.railway_signal_or_gate", "dev.stop_sign", "dev.traffic_signal", "dev.yield_sign", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "DEF-NRS-484A-145 'every sign, signal, marking and device ... placed or erected by a public authority or railroad for the purpose of regulating, warning or guiding traffic': the devices whose direction requires a halt -- dev.stop_sign, dev.yield_sign, dev.traffic_signal with a red indication, dev.railway_signal_or_gate with lights flashing or gate lowering or down -- governing (dev.governs) a travel region the subject occupies. 'official' is the legal status of the device, read from its presence (status reading). Same atoms as the index row 'or a traffic control device,'."}, {"span": "b9", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.sidewalk"], "derived": [], "justification": "st.sidewalk is the 'area for pedestrians between roadway and property line' (DEF-NRS-484A-240 'that portion of a highway between the curb lines or the lateral lines of a highway and the adjacent property lines intended for the use of pedestrians'); it is not a stand-in for a crosswalk, which the words do not name. rel.occupies anchors the subject's footprint on it."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "b3", "standard": "necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic", "concepts": ["rel.ahead_behind_in_lane", "rel.surface_gap"], "params": ["p.queue_halt_gap"], "convention": "a halt is necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic where a road user of traffic is ahead of the halted vehicle in the same lane within the body gap of a queue of halted vehicles", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [{"span": "b10", "why": "Bicycles, electric bicycles and electric scooters are no vehicles under DEF-NRS-484A-320 ('except: (1) Devices moved by human power ... (2) Electric bicycles ... (4) An electric scooter'), so the subject of this duty is never one of them and the duty is the same whether or not the words of subsection 3 hold.", "scope": "none"}], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle. Engaged at an observation where the subject occupies (rel.occupies) an st.sidewalk region and none of the exceptions holds there: no other road user of any class (DEF-NRS-484A-285 'traffic' counts 'pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances') is ahead of the subject in the same lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) with rel.surface_gap at most p.queue_halt_gap; the subject occupies no st.travel_region governed (dev.governs) by a dev.stop_sign, a dev.yield_sign, a dev.traffic_signal showing circular_red, red_arrow or flashing_red, or a dev.railway_signal_or_gate with lights flashing or gate lowering or down; no dev.human_direction of role police_officer indicating stop governs a travel region it occupies; and the halt is not one in compliance with law (operator gap on b4).", "obligation": "drv.motion.complete_halt(subject; p.halt_speed_tolerance) does not hold: the subject is not at rest while on the sidewalk. A halt there is violated.", "params": ["p.halt_speed_tolerance", "p.queue_halt_gap"], "narrowings": [{"span": "b1", "why": "'A person' who stops, stands or parks a vehicle is read through the vehicle's controlled motion, whoever controls it.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "b3", "why": "'necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic' is read only as a halt behind a road user ahead in the same lane within the queue gap; a halt for a crossing road user that is not ahead in the lane is not read as excused.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "b6", "why": "'official traffic-control device' is read from the device's presence on the road, its official status presumed.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "The subject car halts with its front half on a sidewalk across a driveway for 30 s; no road user ahead of it, no device or officer governs the region it occupies; no other road user in the scene."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The subject car crosses a sidewalk at a driveway at 3 m/s without halting."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The subject car halts in the roadway lane, its footprint overlapping no sidewalk."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The subject car is on a sidewalk across a driveway, but kin.speed is not observed on this source, so whether it is at rest is unknown.", "masked": ["kin.speed"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The subject car halts with part of its body on the sidewalk while a police officer's stop direction governs the lane it also occupies."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The subject car halts with part of its body on the sidewalk 2 m behind a halted car ahead of it in the same lane."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.halt_speed_tolerance", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.1, "convention": "the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution", "source": "speed resolution of tracking sources"}, {"name": "p.queue_halt_gap", "unit": "m", "value": 5.0, "convention": "the gap between bodies to a road user ahead in the same lane within which a halt is a halt behind other traffic: the spacing of halted vehicles in a queue", "source": "jam spacing of halted vehicle queues"}], "gaps": [{"span": "b4", "kind": "operator", "proposal": "`compliesWithEngaged` (Formula.compliesWithEngaged (binder map)): an operator that decides whether, at an observation, the subject's present conduct is required by some rule of the accepted set that is engaged for the subject there and is complied with by that conduct, so that a halt 'in compliance with law' is a halt some engaged rule requires of the subject (a stop at a sign, a yield to oncoming traffic or to an emergency vehicle, a stop for a school bus); it decides the time and the reason of the halt the law excuses", "nearest": "dev.governs, dev.stop_sign, dev.traffic_signal, rel.occupies, st.travel_region read only the halts a governing device requires; Formula.rule and Formula.ruleApplies compose one named rule each, never 'law' as the set of all rules engaged for the subject"}], "gap_resolutions": []}
