 intersection' (DEF-NRS-484A-105 'the area embraced within the prolongation or connection of the lateral curb lines ... The junction of an alley with a street, road or highway shall not constitute an intersection'); not a stand-in for a crosswalk or a stop line. rel.occupies anchors the subject's footprint within it. Same mapping as the index row 'within an intersection'."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "b3", "standard": "necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic", "concepts": ["rel.ahead_behind_in_lane", "rel.surface_gap"], "params": ["p.queue_halt_gap"], "convention": "a halt is necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic where a road user of traffic is ahead of the halted vehicle in the same lane within the body gap of a queue of halted vehicles", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "subject", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "The subject is a vehicle. Engaged at an observation where the subject occupies (rel.occupies) an st.intersection region and none of the exceptions holds there: no other road user of any class (DEF-NRS-484A-285 'traffic' counts 'pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances') is ahead of the subject in the same lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) with rel.surface_gap at most p.queue_halt_gap; the subject occupies no st.travel_region (the intersection included) governed (dev.governs) by a dev.stop_sign, a dev.yield_sign, a dev.traffic_signal showing circular_red, red_arrow or flashing_red, or a dev.railway_signal_or_gate with lights flashing or gate lowering or down; no dev.human_direction of role police_officer indicating stop governs a travel region it occupies; and the halt is not one in compliance with law (operator gap on b4).", "obligation": "drv.motion.complete_halt(subject; p.halt_speed_tolerance) does not hold: the subject is not at rest while within the intersection. A halt 